  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1222 PM CDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nThe cutoff low will become more compact and gradually track eastward \non Saturday over southern AZ. Despite leading shortwaves out ahead \nof it, the moisture fetch will likely not reach the TX/NM border \nuntil Saturday evening, thus much of the area will remain dry for \nthe day. Temperatures will be about 3-5 degrees cooler under mostly \ncloudy skies. As the low moves over the Four Corners region, showers \nand thunderstorms will finally begin to encompass most areas on the \nCaprock before continuing to track eastward into the evening. The \nupper low will track due east once it reaches Colorado and \nprecipitation looks to overspread the entire area Monday along the \nassociated surface cold front. Showers and thunderstorms will taper \noff from north to south on Tuesday as the low and front depart the \nregion. The overall severe threat looks to be low, however locally \nheavy rainfall/flooding are possible, particularly with any training \nthunderstorms. Although forecast confidence is increasing, there \nremains uncertainty as to the exact timing and position of the \nheaviest rainfall. Stay tuned for updates.",
